(7155450, 1096574, 60173, '<td valign="top">I wouldn''t have expected this much glare from a 40mm, unless it were really dirty. If this is a result of a dirty lens, then I would recommend NOT cleaning it, because I love me some sun glare! <br/> <br/>This image fits perfectly with the feeling I get when geese first start migrating every year. It''s a haunting distant "what is that...." sound that gains quickly in intensity. Soon they''re right on you and the racket is undeniable. Canadians are invading! <br/> <br/>Yes, yes indeed. This is what it will look like when Canada attacks...</td>', 'I wouldn''t have expected this much glare from a 40mm, unless it were really dirty. If this is a result of a dirty lens, then I would recommend NOT cleaning it, because I love me some sun glare!  This image fits perfectly with the feeling I get when geese first start migrating every year. It''s a haunting distant "what is that...." sound that gains quickly in intensity. Soon they''re right on you and the racket is undeniable. Canadians are invading!  Yes, yes indeed. This is what it will look like when Canada attacks...', '2014-01-10 12:43:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7155665, 1096248, 161988, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Violetz:</b></div><hr/><i> Tree lights and city lights, did the water have a reflection of the trees? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well here''s the thing.  That''s not water in front of the tree''s. It''s just cement. When the lights bounced off the cement it turned this beautiful golden color.<br/> <br/>Now this cement area is much larger and when I framed up this shot I had the entire height of the tree''s reflected off the cement area.  It looked absolutely beautiful (in the camera).  However, when I got home and put it on the computer I realized you could see all the imperfections of the cement.  The cracks, the holes, the discolorations etc. etc.  It looked like hell.<br/> <br/>I had to get the entry in that evening and had basically ran out of time.  So I cropped the hell out of it and it just ruined the entire look of the picture.  What are you gonna do? Such is life.<br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments however.</td>', 'Originally posted by Violetz: Tree lights and city lights, did the water have a reflection of the trees?   Well here''s the thing.  That''s not water in front of the tree''s. It''s just cement. When the lights bounced off the cement it turned this beautiful golden color. Now this cement area is much larger and when I framed up this shot I had the entire height of the tree''s reflected off the cement area.  It looked absolutely beautiful (in the camera).  However, when I got home and put it on the computer I realized you could see all the imperfections of the cement.  The cracks, the holes, the discolorations etc. etc.  It looked like hell. I had to get the entry in that evening and had basically ran out of time.  So I cropped the hell out of it and it just ruined the entire look of the picture.  What are you gonna do? Such is life. Thanks for your comments however.', '2014-01-10 22:46:28.000000', NULL, 0),
